---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Press &amp; Researchers | Tom Pickup"
  description="Method, data and contact routes for journalists covering Lancashire County Council, Burnley, and council spending. Every published figure traces to a checkable document."
>
  <section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <h1>Press &amp; Researchers</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">For journalists, producers and researchers covering Lancashire</p>

      <div class="legal-content">
        <h2>Who I Am</h2>
        <p>
          Tom Pickup. Lancashire County Councillor for Padiham &amp; Burnley West, elected
          May 2025. Cabinet Member for Adult Social Care. Reform UK.
        </p>

        <h2>How the Figures Are Sourced</h2>
        <p>
          Every figure I publish traces to a primary document. That means council
          spending files, committee papers, statements of accounts, Companies House
          filings, or Electoral Commission records. Each figure is checked at the source
          before it goes out. The source is named on the asset. If a number is modelled
          rather than official, it says so.
        </p>
        <p>
          "Over &pound;500" transparency data is not a council's total budget, and I say
          so wherever it appears. Spend and purchase orders are never summed together.
        </p>

        <h2>Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          If you find an error, tell me and it gets corrected quickly and plainly. A
          correction is permanent; a wrong number defended is worse.
        </p>

        <h2>What You Can Use</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Council spending data:</strong> <a href="https://aidoge.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI DOGE</a> holds
            22 million spending transactions across dozens of English councils. Search by
            supplier, category or council. Every figure comes from each council's own
            published transparency files.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Analysis on this site:</strong> articles under
            <a href="/doge/">DOGE</a> and <a href="/lancs/">Lancashire</a> carry their
            sources inline. Quote with attribution.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Comment:</strong> for Lancashire County Council official business,
            contact the council&rsquo;s press office. For comment in a personal or party
            capacity, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or X
            (<a href="https://x.com/tompickup" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@tompickup</a>).
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Response Times</h2>
        <p>
          Same day for anything on deadline where I can. Say you are press in the subject
          line.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding: 7rem 0 var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .legal-page h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .legal-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--separator);
  }

  .legal-content h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .legal-content p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal-content ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal-content ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 20px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .legal-content ul li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 10px;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .legal-content a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .legal-content strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .legal-page {
      padding: 6rem 0 var(--space-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
